{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The proverbs of Solomon</b> etc. — This is the section of admonition; he declares in it the excellence of primordial Wisdom, for through it something was created from nothing, and he admonishes to cleave to it and to turn away from the rejected woman, and he demonstrates to put to death Folly and the desire of the one formed from the earth, and to give life to the blameless soul." "<b>Son of David</b> — To tell his excellence, that he was the son of a wise and discerning man." "<b>King</b> — For because of their wisdom both of them reigned over Israel; or that he was a king with a wise and understanding one, and <b>king</b> is an epithet, like עבד ארך אפים (long-suffering)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra writes עבד ארך אבר, apparently a textual variant or corruption for the standard עבד ארך אפים (Exodus 34:7); rendered hyper-literally as it appears."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:20:43.355990161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}